# Postposed daypart words that put a bare 12-hour clock reading into the
# afternoon/evening half (meridiem offset +12), exactly as the de locale's
# "nachmittags"/"abends" already do.  These are the Dutch genitive surfaces
# that trail a clock reading after the fossilised "'s" particle
# ("acht uur 's avonds" == 20:00, "drie uur 's middags" == 15:00).
# Bands: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale nl -- middag/afternoon
# [12:00, 18:00) and avond/evening [18:00, 24:00) are the pm half.
middags
avonds
